+No P0s. The queue design is mechanically safe, but the plan needs rework because its cost premise is false and several independent contracts are missing.
+
+- **P1 — Decision 1 relies on caching that does not exist.** The plan says most of Relations’ input will use a prefix cached by the other import jobs ([plan:50](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/plans/261005d-marginalia-out-of-the-experimental-switch.md:50>)). Current policy explicitly says no two distinct stages share an article cache ([step-order.ts:81](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/step-order.ts:81>)), and Relations specifically “shares a cached article with nothing” because its schema differs ([models.ts:1958](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/models.ts:1958>)). Production one-call stages currently record zero cache reads/writes, and cross-job cache coordination is deliberately absent ([prompt-caching.md:242](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/prompt-caching.md:242>)). This decision adds one cold capable-tier call to every default import. Re-state the decision using the full measured marginal cost, without a cache discount.
+
+- **P1 — The server-side queue contract and its independent test are omitted.** The production integration test deliberately copies the current seven requests rather than importing the list ([publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:21](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:21>), [publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:121](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:121>)). It must gain `["relations"]` between Ideas and Simple and change seven to eight. This suite is the evidence that all import paths, opt-out, ordering, work-key joining, free status and transaction rollback still work. The authoritative queue documentation also enumerates the jobs and omits Marginalia ([ingest-queue.md:618](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/ingest-queue.md:618>)).
+
+- **P2 — Several exact tests and generated artefacts need named changes, not the plan’s generic sweep.**
+  
+  - The three separate assertions for reader copy, requests and queue grouping all need Relations ([auto-modes.test.tsx:198](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/auto-modes.test.tsx:198>), [auto-modes.test.tsx:206](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/auto-modes.test.tsx:206>), [auto-modes.test.tsx:225](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/auto-modes.test.tsx:225>)).
+  - The switch-off Dock case currently expects the closed Marginalia toggle to disappear; it must instead expect a visible, unpressed toggle ([dock-experimental-modes.test.tsx:258](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/dock-experimental-modes.test.tsx:258>)).
+  - The first-open wiring case explicitly expects switch-off to produce Summary alone, and its surrounding descriptions still say the switch decides ([first-open-default-wiring.test.tsx:3](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/first-open-default-wiring.test.tsx:3>), [first-open-default-wiring.test.tsx:88](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/first-open-default-wiring.test.tsx:88>)).
+  - The command-pick catalogue definitely is compared exactly, so “if” is wrong. Marginalia must gain the `owner-article-experimental-off` context in [command-pick-catalogue.generated.json:389](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/command-pick-catalogue.generated.json:389>); the gate is [command-pick-catalogue.test.ts:269](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/command-pick-catalogue.test.ts:269>). The eval answer snapshot uses the switch-on context and should remain unchanged.
+
+- **P2 — The newly reachable signed-out visitor press needs direct network coverage.** The signed-out sweep excludes toggles from `modeRadios`, then opens `?margin=1` and tests only the on→off press ([public-network-trace.test.tsx:1988](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/public-network-trace.test.tsx:1988>), [public-network-trace.test.tsx:2036](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/public-network-trace.test.tsx:2036>)). Once the default bar exposes Marginalia, test the unpressed toggle from a bare public page, click off→on and on→off, and assert no private request or non-GET. The signed-in non-owner test already covers both presses, but only with Experimental on ([public-network-trace.test.tsx:2919](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/public-network-trace.test.tsx:2919>)).
+
+- **P2 — Reader-facing help and origin copy will be false.** `/help` does not only derive a tag: it explicitly calls Marginalia experimental ([help-topics.tsx:140](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/help/help-topics.tsx:140>)), while the existing help test checks only the derived heading/table tags and will not catch that sentence ([help-page.test.tsx:224](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/help-page.test.tsx:224>)). Relation-word cards say they were made when the reader turned Marginalia on ([tips.ts:77](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/marginalia/tips.ts:77>)), and the catalogue’s shared tooltip says turning it on causes the model pass ([mode-catalog.ts:643](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/mode-catalog.ts:643>)); both become false for imported results and were already false for visitors. `/features` needs no manual edit: its tag and test are derived from the catalogue ([FeaturesPage.tsx:33](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/FeaturesPage.tsx:33>), [features-page-modes.test.tsx:120](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/features-page-modes.test.tsx:120>)).
+
+- **P2 — Governing docs omitted or underspecified.** The missing entry-point doc says Marginalia is behind the switch twice and generates nothing ([reading-view-overview.md:9](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/reading-view-overview.md:9>), [reading-view-overview.md:159](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/reading-view-overview.md:159>)). `mode.md` says Marginalia has nothing to generate and that promoting a mode is “the whole of the behaviour”; this change disproves both statements ([mode.md:107](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/mode.md:107>), [mode.md:344](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/mode.md:344>)). The named `marginalia.md` edit must replace “the press … and nothing else” ([marginalia.md:115](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/marginalia.md:115>)); `interface-vision.md` must update not just gating but “shows only what other modes made” ([interface-vision.md:156](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/docs/project/interface-vision.md:156>)).
+
+- **P3 — Source comments remain stale, and `STEP_ORDER` already contains Relations.** No membership edit to `STEP_ORDER` is needed; Relations is already there, but its comment says an owner’s press starts it ([step-order.ts:117](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/step-order.ts:117>)). Also update the mode inventory in [auto-mode-steps.ts:24](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/auto-mode-steps.ts:24>), both stale Dock comments ([Dock.tsx:1038](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/Dock.tsx:1038>), [Dock.tsx:2861](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/Dock.tsx:2861>)), and the first-open comments and now-unused `on` dependency in [last-view.ts:49](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/last-view.ts:49>), [last-view.ts:493](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/last-view.ts:493>) and [last-view.ts:609](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/last-view.ts:609>). The press-path comments in `useRelations`, `activation` and `MarginaliaColumn` remain accurate for missing legacy/opted-out articles, but must stop implying it is the only production path.
+
+Safety conclusions:
+
+- Decision 1’s queue mechanics are safe: publication queues only for the importing owner and respects `auto_modes_off_at` ([pg-revisions.ts:2437](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/store/pg-revisions.ts:2437>), [pg-revisions.ts:2507](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/store/pg-revisions.ts:2507>)); Relations is a sharing step with no dependencies ([sharing-steps.ts:80](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/sharing-steps.ts:80>)); short articles store an empty result without a model call ([relations.ts:400](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/relations.ts:400>)); and successor jobs carry no ingest reservation/quota slot ([publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:463](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/publication-queues-the-main-modes.test.ts:463>)). I found no runtime billing, lease-budget or queue code assuming seven.
+- Decision 2 applies to any signed-in reader, including a signed-in non-owner, because `firstOpenHref` checks sign-in rather than ownership ([last-view.ts:545](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/last-view.ts:545>)). That is consistent with `POLICY.marginalia: available` ([visitor.ts:193](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/visitor.ts:193>)). An owner’s arrival mounts five artefact GETs, including Relations, but sends no job POST ([artefact-read-hooks.test.tsx:159](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/tests/artefact-read-hooks.test.tsx:159>)); therefore it spends no money.
+- A visitor press cannot arm a job because Dock passes `arms = false` for visitors ([Dock.tsx:1898](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/Dock.tsx:1898>)), and the owner-only feed is not mounted ([Reader.tsx:3367](</home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbvv54j2-marginalia-not-experimental/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:3367>)). It changes the URL and draws from the existing public payload; omitted relation words are handled as `null`.
+
+VERDICT: rework
